[1st pudding sacrifice]
The black pudding corpse disappears in a burst of flame --more--
an object appears at your feet --more--

[3rd pudding sacrifice]
The black pudding corpse disappears in a burst of flame --more--
Your ring of slow digestion glows softly amber --more--

[6th pudding sacrifice]
You hear Anhur yawn --more--
The black pudding corpse disappears in a disappointing fizzle of flame.

[10th pudding sacrifice]
Nothing happens.

[sacrifice a passing goblin]
The goblin corpse disappears in a burst of flame --more--
an object appears at your feet --more--

OK, so this could easily be circumvented with Create Monster, or even
by waiting for random monsters to appear, but it would break things up
a little and force the player to take on some different monsters. It
also doesn't address the "death drop" issue at all, so on it's own it
wouldn't be enough to deter pudding exploitation, but perhaps it could
be used in conjunction with some of the other ideas suggested.


